<rml>
<head>
	<!-- The private shop signs (uiprivateshopbuilder.py
	     PrivateShopAdvertisementBoard): one sign over each open private shop,
	     its name centered on the shop owner's position raised 220 units and
	     projected (chr.GetProjectPosition). While the shop-signs flag is on,
	     the Interface makes one facade per sign, nui_shop_signs.ShopSign
	     (controller assets/root/nui_shop_signs.py), and every sign is an entry
	     of this one document (spec D18). Each anchor places itself every
	     frame, where legacy positioned each sign from Python every frame; the
	     game option that hides the signs of other players reaches the
	     document through the system.show_sales_text feed. A release of the
	     left button on a sign opens the shop (net.SendOnClickPacket). The
	     names are shown as written, their color tags drawn and links not
	     (nui-text links="off"). Each repeated slot binds nothing: RmlUi
	     updates a repeated element's own views with the data-for that removes
	     it. The classic thin board art is under d:/ymir work/ (assets/ETC). -->
	<title>shop-signs</title>
	<link type="text/template" href="../../nui.rtpl"/>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="shop-signs.rcss"/>
</head>
<body template="nui" class="nui-overlay nui-below-legacy-ui shop-signs" data-model="shop_signs">
	<div class="shop-signs__slot" data-for="s : signs">
		<nui-anchor class="shop-signs__anchor" mode="project" height="220" data-attr-vid="s.vid"
			data-attr-id="'shop-sign-' + s.vid" data-if="s.shown &amp;&amp; (show_all || s.own)"><div
			class="nui-panel shop-sign nui-interactive" data-style---legacy-width="s.legacy_width" data-event-mouseup="open(s.vid, ev.button)"><nui-text
			class="shop-sign__text" links="off" data-attr-value="s.text"/></div></nui-anchor>
	</div>
</body>
</rml>
